  "html": "<div id=\"questionExplanation-61801\" class=\"questionExplanation\" style=\"display: block;\"><p>The vertices of a polyhedron are the corners where edges meet.</p>\n<p>The rectangular prism has <mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"4\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c32\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container> vertices in total, as shown below. </p>\n<div id=\"graphic-q-61801-e-0\" class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/q-61801-e-0\"></div> </div>",
